output:
 Iran carried out ' eye for eye' punishment where a man convicted acid attack was blinded in one eye. This punishment is believed to be Iran first case of Qasas, meaning retribution in kind. Amnesty International denounced the sentence as exposing Iran justice system brutality, and pro prohibited by international law punishment. 

- Iran Carried out eye for an eye punishment, blinded man convicted acid attack convict in eye;
- punishment believed to be first of retribution in kind, man was blinded in left eye with right eye still to be blinded, man was also sentenced to 10 years prison and ordered to pay blood money;
- Amnesty international denounced punishment as brutal and inhuman and prohibited by international law punishment
